    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 509,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Buddy cop film\nWhile the movie in itself was a buddy cop film ( i.e. pairing a fictional cop with a real world boy ) , the film 's police department obligatorily assigned all cops a conflicting buddy to work with , even to the extreme of one officer being partnered with a cartoon cat . A subgenre of the buddy cop film is the buddy cop-dog movie , which teams a cop with a dog , but uses the same element of unlikely partnership to create comedic hijinks . Examples include Turner & Hooch , Top Dog and K-9 ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
